From eb0ebe8139c5990f8083d392a5f275ff0145235e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:19:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Gold-standard architecture: no objectives, free discussion,
 ambiguous evidence
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Play-testing found the forced investigation-round sequence made the game
too easy. This redesigns the core loop without touching the 11 existing
built-in stories, the custom story builder, the voting system, the
launcher icon, or RTL handling.

CORE RULE (new): everyone knows something, everyone hides something, but
only the guilty character's secret is directly connected to the crime.

StoryCharacter.java:
- Added a lean 6-arg constructor (name, profession, publicIdentity,
  secret, knowledge, guilty) for new content -- no objective, no
  statement, no separate crime objective. The original 9-arg constructor
  is untouched and still backs all 11 existing built-in stories plus any
  already-saved custom stories; both shapes now coexist on one class.

MainActivity.java:
- roleReveal(): objective/statement/crimeObjective panels are now shown
  only when non-empty, so the new lean characters don't display blank
  panels while the 11 existing stories (whose data is still non-empty)
  render exactly as before.
- Replaced the forced investigationStep() round-by-round sequence with
  freeDiscussion() (a hub: reveal more evidence, or go straight to
  voting -- player's choice) and evidenceReveal() (shows one piece of
  public evidence, returns to the hub). This reuses the *same*
  GameManager/InvestigationRound data and state (investigationIndex,
  currentInvestigationRound(), investigationFinished()) that the old
  flow used -- only the UI-level sequencing changed, not the data model,
  per "do not perform a destructive rewrite." This also applies to the
  11 existing stories' evidence, which directly addresses the
  play-testing complaint for the whole app, not just the new story.

Story.java:
- Added an optional StoryIntroduction parameter to the fixed-cast
  constructor (defaults to the old generic filler when omitted, so the
  existing custom() factory used by the real custom-story builder and by
  CustomStoryStore is 100% unchanged) plus a private builtIn() factory
  for built-in fixed-cast stories.
- Added ONE new gold-standard story to catalog(): "نخب أخير" (gala
  poisoning), fixed at exactly 6 players / 1 guilty. All 6 characters
  use the new lean shape. 4 evidence pieces, each written to plausibly
  implicate more than one character (verified by a test that greps
  every evidence string for every character's name). A full customEnding
  covering who/what/why/how/which evidence/why each innocent looked
  suspicious.

GameManagerTest.java: updated the general character-shape sweep to only
check the fields every story guarantees; added a dedicated legacy-shape
regression test for the other 11 stories; added structural tests for the
new story's character shape, evidence ambiguity, and confirmed voting is
never gated by how much evidence has been revealed. 12/12 tests pass.

Not touched: CustomStoryStore.java, Player.java, GameManager.java (data/
state layer, reused as-is), InvestigationRound.java, InvestigationData.java,
Clue.java, StoryIntroduction.java, the custom story builder UI, the
launcher icon, AndroidManifest.xml, colors.xml, strings.xml. No Question
Cards, no detective/special roles beyond what already existed, no
branching endings, no online features.

Known limitation: the custom story builder UI still collects
statement/objective/crimeObjective fields (unchanged) -- the brief's own
'eventually support' phrasing for the builder was treated as forward-
looking prep, not an immediate rewrite, consistent with 'do not rewrite
the entire application' and 'first create ONE gold-standard story.'
